==English==

===Etymology===
From  {{etyl|frm|en}}, {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|percussion|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|percussiō||striking|lang=la}}, from {{term|percutiō||I strike|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|percussions}}

# {{context|countable|lang=en}} the [[collision]] of two [[bodies]] in order to produce a [[sound]]
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} the sound so produced
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} the [[detonation]] of a [[percussion cap]] in a [[firearm]]
# {{context|medicine|lang=en}} the [[tapping]] of the [[body]] as an aid to [[medical]] [[diagnosis]]
# {{context|music|lang=en}} the section of an [[orchestra]] or band containing [[percussion instrument]]s; such instruments considered as a group
# {{context|engineering|lang=en}} the repeated striking of an object to break or shape it, as in percussion drilling

